    "turn_text": "I think it's pretty well known in the United States. Again, it's not an exotic thing. It's sort of part of our culture here, probably slightly well known, better known than other scholarships, like the Marshall Scholarship, for example, which sends a lot of Americans to the UK as well. So no, it's not something that requires a lot of advertisement. If you're doing well in university and are involved in extracurriculars and maybe have some form of athletic activity that you do, it's one of those things that occurs to you at a minimum.",
