    "turn_text": "Exactly. No matter how ascetic you may be, you get used to a certain level of compensation. I was helped by some external factors, including 9-11. My offices at Goldman Sachs were literally three blocks away from the World Trade Center. when we were struck with that terrorist attack on 9-11 of 2001. First of all, the business collapsed subsequently with the economy, so that in some ways made it easier to think about alternatives. But also, it was one of those moments where you realize tomorrow is really promised to no man. And so a number of things came together at that point to say, hey, think back to what you thought you might want to do and maybe take some steps to get there.",
