    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74126.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 78,
    "turn_text": "Oh, okay. So you want to move on to the second cataclysm that we're dealing with concurrently here, do you? Yeah, right. I mean, we forget in the aftermath of that insurrection against the Capitol, we forget we're in the middle of a brutal, brutal global pandemic here. Yeah. And of course, what you saw was precisely that, you know, I'll never forget. My first inauguration was Barack Obama in January of 2009 and very literally millions of people as far as the eye could see on the mall there all the way back to the Potomac River. And now it was just, it was an armed camp because of what had happened two weeks earlier. And yes, you know, we weren't obviously best practices that we not sit next to each other. So, you know, you basically had the Congress of the United States, the diplomatic corps and the president's friends and family. And so yeah, it was a very, it was a very somber moment.",
