    "turn_idx": 101,
    "turn_text": "You know, honestly, I haven't spent enough time and really sort of scrutinized the curriculum or what people are doing. I will tell you one change that I've noticed in the hall. This is actually, I think, a good thing, particularly for a college that isn't one of the wealthier colleges. Oxford, and I think in general, but certainly the hall has gotten an awful lot smarter about the dreaded development office, right? And here in the United States, we're used to, you know, you're about three days into your freshman year in college before your college starts asking you for money beyond the tuition that you're paying. And I actually think that's a really good thing. I mean, let's face it, all of us get educations at places like Teddy Hall that are far, far more valuable than what we pay for them. So I think the tradition, and I know it's annoying to get those letters and those phone calls, but the tradition of then supporting your college or your university so that The people who come behind you can have a good or better experience as you had is a wonderful thing. And yes, I think Teddy Hall in the sort of 25 years I've been watching it has really come into the 21st century in terms of development, making sure that it's financially stable with the help of its graduates.",
